    "sha": "d1eb8a1bcc8e37b31dca7b0679951a2a2659ef44",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOV1WsOtoAKGQxZWI4YTFiY2M4ZTM3YjMxZGNhN2IwNjc5OTUxYTJhMjY1OWVmNDQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T03:02:03Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Quintin Smits",
        "email": "qd.smits@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T03:02:03Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(tools): tool component bodies from STEP, STL and OBJ files\n\nA tool component's body now comes from a mesh file, placed by its own\nISO 13399 mounting frame:\n\n- camcraft-geometry classifies MCS_INSERT as CsysRole::Mounting (the\n  app's step_csys.rs re-exports it); a file with MCS and MCS_INSERT is\n  ambiguous and refused by find().\n- camcraft_tools::mesh_body::MeshBody reads a STEP body through the\n  kernel import with its coordinate systems, or an STL/OBJ body\n  (new mesh_file reader) with stored frames. Ports and the CIP are\n  read in the mounting frame; one that is not below it is refused.\n- spindle_geometry() gives a ComponentBody: the revolved envelope,\n  drawn as a stepped outline that only grows it and is checked to\n  enclose it. lathe_geometry() gives a LatheBody for resolve_lathe.\n- A meshed STEP body grows by the certified chord deviation: spindle\n  bands, and the lathe clearance through LatheClearance::padded.\n- One body is at most 1 000 000 facets; past it the body is refused by\n  name (#1041). Corrupt or degenerate files are refused by name.\n\nRefs #3643\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
